d dining tower; connect its copper hip to the north roof with raised tiled slopes and matching ridge adornment. Follow-up 8 October 2026: raise the courtyard dining-tower upper glazing to align with the north-wing upper windows, shortening the copper cap while retaining period-appropriate sash divisions. Follow-up 9 October 2026 UTC: correct the front west gable angle and rear section width against the supplied west and northwest images, then validate against both photographs before merging to dev. Later 9 October correction: restore the west wing's full-height level ridge, simple front and rear gables, and matching courtyard awning; the lowered rear roof and exposed courtyard wall are a regression. Follow-up15October2026: prioritize a straight north-wing ridge through the west-wing junction, move the west peak to achieve a right-angle intersection, and compare the remaining roof features and northeast copper coverage against the supplied overhead views. Follow-up16October2026: photograph-match the Prairie entry lower side reveals, shaped header, one inset step and recessed decorative field; distinguish the recessed entrance from lower stones that slope outward.","counts":{"claims":14,"entities":1,"grades":[[0,1,13],[0,1,0]]},"date":"2026-09-29","has_archive_link":false,"source_id":"owner_glessner_v4_reconstruction_brief_2026","tier":5,"type":"dataset","use":"other_scene"},{"citation":"Papers of Abraham Lincoln, Act to Incorporate Chicago","counts":{"claims":2,"entities":2,"grades":[[0,2,0],[0,2,0]]},"date":"accessed 2026-09-01","has_archive_link":false,"source_id":"pal_chicago_incorporation_1835","tier":4,"type":"website","use":"scene"},{"citation":"Papers of Abraham Lincoln, person record: Gholson Kercheval","counts":{"claims":0,"entities":0,"grades":[[0,0,0],[0,0,0]]},"date":"accessed 2026-09-02","has_archive_link":false,"source_id":"pal_gholson_kercheval","tier":4,"type":"website","use":"unused"},{"citation":"Papers of Abraham Lincoln, Giles Spring person record