ce it draws — every dimension on the fence layer is invented, and the liberties register L129 says so","a Lombardy poplar anywhere in Chicago but this one group","a view of the 1835 fort in panel 8: that panel is dated 1830 by the sheet's own key and was mistaken for a fort plate for a month"],"what_it_supplies":["panel 1: Old Fort Dearborn of 1803 from across the river - the palisade under a ruled cap line, the barracks ranges, the blockhouses and the bare trodden ground outside the walls that the fort dearborn apron data is built on","panel 8: the town from the lake in 1830, population 96 - the low far bank, a lodge and bark canoes on the shore, and trees round the buildings on both banks; a scene-adjacent TOWN view, five years early, not a second view of the fort","panel 12: the long low Kinzie house with a full-width piazza on its front, a red roof, and outbuildings up the rise behind it","panel 12: a row of four Lombardy poplars standing between the house and the river — the count and rhythm the planted rows generator measures across seven plates","panel 12: PICKET-FENCED garden plots at the house — close-set vertical pales, the treatment the town dooryard pickets data deals to the town's house lots","panel 12: the fenced green between house and water that Wau-Bun describes in words, drawn","panel 11: the Green Tree Hotel as a two-storey clapboard block with end chimneys and even sash, with ship masts behind it","panel 5: Fort Dearborn as rebuilt 1835 — picket palisade, galleried barracks range, blockhouse; the blockhouse's four-sided cap carries a small square cupola at its centre, under a little cap of its own, and the panel draws no separate stack anywhere on that roof. FORM ONLY, as every line of this sheet is: the cupola's size, height and detail are not in it, and the absence of a stack in a retrospective chromolithograph is not testimony that the building had no flue","panel 14: the Sauganash Hotel as a two-storey clapboard block with an attached single-storey log wing and no full-width gallery","the sheet's printed key, which names each panel and dates several of the buildings"]},"uses":["scene","other_scene"]}
