+# First Fort Dearborn: finite original-scope coverage, 2026-11-10
+
+This re-reading accounts for all **21 original records and nine existing context records**, plus every picture/container listed on original T-2387 and retained by T-3041. It adds no geometry, source, rights finding or historical optical claim. Source/identity dispositions below are separate from the actual native image verdicts.
+
+T-3041 records the T-3335 owner instruction: **“Keep Whistler’s measured plan for everything else … blockhouse proportions, the main gate as a gap between the barracks halves (no gate building), range functions and lengths, chimneys.”** The four adopted exceptions are already built: both roof cupolas (including later owner refinements), the magazine barrel vault, the north-east small-house pyramid and both western wickets. Do not reopen those landed fixes from old partial prose.
+
+The exact [30-row matrix](coverage-original21-context9-20261110.json) keeps each record’s current name, original/context membership and separate Currey, Kurz panel1, Lossing, Whistler and four held-preview dispositions. The [source/date/use inventory](source-coverage-rights-dates-20261110.json) records actual picture reads and hashes, including each held preview and the source container’s four images. `stable_middle` remains the **house in the factor’s department**, from Whistler numeral23. The covered way is expressly omitted from Whistler’s drawing (index33); Currey’s dashed line records a route, not its four reconstructed runs. The wharf does have a dotted mark/index27; its river seat and minimum deck remain reconstructed.
+
+## All 30 component dispositions
+
+| Existing record | Set | Currey | Kurz panel1 | Lossing |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `first_fort_dearborn_blockhouse_nw` | original | adopted form / owner plan | owner plan / limited identity | compound silhouette |
