+
+## Named picture differences have finite dispositions
+
+Kurz’s central tower cluster, range overlap and compressed staff disagree with Whistler’s measured corner layout. They are retained under the explicit owner plan choice and T-3153 source/camera tolerance. The lower-right two-storey galleried house is visible, but no named context identity is established; it is **not individually identified**, rather than a newly missing factory/agent/stable to invent. Hidden faces and the second picket row are not independently resolved by that panel. These are review dispositions, not permission to accept unseen geometry.
+
+Lossing’s full uncropped960×506 engraving actually shows a distant fort beside the prominent foreground Kinzie house. The existing Kinzie-fit world camera puts fort samples beyondx2038..4244, outside the960px source. It remains unchanged. The new independent `lossing_1869_fort` diagnostic frames the unchanged14coremembers against the fort silhouette atx445..850. Holding a virtual1600px focal length,5.75m review eye and128° heading, only range and principal point frame that envelope; no lens or historic viewpoint is recovered and no world placement is fitted. All actual14MASTER vertices project within the source: x444.50..850.25, y57.38..262.24. The full75ftstaff projects nearx644/y57 whereas the drawing places its top aroundx540/y100. That source/plan/camera conflict is within tolerance; the measured staff is retained.
+
+One genuine external native-model comparison was rendered and directly inspected from the pinned14currentmasters: the fort occupies the intended distant area, both existing cupolas and the stockade are visible, and the documented plan produces the declared skyline/flag disagreement. Raw PNG, full pair, exact source/model/camera/sidecar hashes and exit0 receipt are retained in `history/20261110-before-final-coverage/`. Its proposed canonical record is **unreviewed** pending the parent’s A5 native control audit and final B review. This is a comparison baseline, not a final accepted match or a published runtime test.
+
+The four Getty previews were each actually viewed. They show related prints/paintings with different river approaches, tower/range compositions and outside galleries; neither their independence nor original publication/copy rights is established here. The held Chicagology container’s attributed1857 sketch, related engraving, Whistler reproduction and Earle painting were also viewed. Their rights findings remain unchanged. No camera, source-photo derivative, model shape or material colour is derived from these held copies. The separately qualified public-domain witnesses provide the allowed comparisons; held-copy accounting creates no arbitrary geometry or never-ending follow-up.
+
+## Final review boundary
+
+Current Currey/Kurz cameras, matches, actual raw renders and full pairs are preserved before this coverage pass. Currey’s existing bounded acceptance and its crop/context limits are unchanged. Kurz stays `differs` until the actual current comparison is re-adjudicated under the owner plan. Lossing stays `unreviewed`; no matching verdict is inherited from a house camera, CPU envelope fit or older geometry. After the parent’s combined native audit, use actual current bindings/comparisons and published desktop/phone checks to record the finite original-scope acceptance. No new geometry or photo follow-up is requested by this matrix.
+
+## Final adopted-native image adjudication
+
+The A5 native control audit passed and all four current fort comparisons were then genuinely rendered and directly reviewed, each exit0: northwest Currey14, outer-picket Currey14, Kurz30 and Lossing14. The existing Currey matches were maintained in a separate shared-native refresh; its northwest raw differs at only6pixels and its outer-picket full pair is pixel-identical. Lossing before/after raw PNGs are pixel-identical. Current source/model/camera/group bindings are written by those real renders. The named finite Kurz/Lossing rows are now accepted: retained measured plan/staff underT3335, source/camera discrepancy withinT3153, and unlabelled outside gallery not individually identified with any named record. No geometry, rights or source dates change. All30existing records and every originally listed picture/container have an explicit disposition; none is held to a tiny unresolved composite identity. This is final image-scope acceptance, with published terrain/walking/runtime checks and formal ticket/PR completion remaining parent-owned.
