+# Second Fort Dearborn: finite every-building comparison (T-2388)
+
+This rereads the original 21-record scope for **1 July 1835**. The machine-readable
+[coverage matrix](coverage.json) names every record, every cleared picture actually
+opened, source hashes, dated interpretation and the remaining rendering qualification.
+It is a rereading of the existing corpus, not a new archival count.
+
+Four finite physical omissions are completed: the officers' outside stair, the plan-named
+big barn's cupola, Kinzie's additional small posterns, and the securely keyed
+commandant's front double gallery through an explicit reconstructed continuity choice. The already-built officers'
+upper piazza receives one outside timber stair. Hubbard expressly describes exterior stairs in his 1818 account
+(autobiography, printed p.36, leaf74, text2353–2358). Its continuity into July1835 has
+exactly the conditional interpretation already carried by the existing gallery.
+The stair's right/south-end position and every dimension are reconstructed. Unknown
+location does not prevent a bounded reconstruction: the prior refusal is explicitly
+superseded. Neither the gallery nor the blockhouse cupola is duplicated.
+
+The barn cupola is1.2m square, a plain boarded body with its eave1.0m above the
+existing ridge and a0.45m pyramid cap. Only occurrence is attested by the literal
+plan label; shape, dimensions and ridge midpoint are declared liberties. A new
+explicit outbuilding opt-in avoids activating other old descriptive cupola booleans.
+
+The actual Wau-Bun ch.XVII paragraph was independently fetched/read10November2026:
+“Large gates opened to the north and south, and there were small posterns here and
+there for the accommodation of the inmates.” The small openings are additional.
+Two is the minimum plural: east/west sides,1.5m widths, clear seats at localv41.0m
+and11.5m, leaf carpentry and swing are reconstructed. Existing main north/south
+gates retain their3.6m spans. Actual native gate controls and the app hanging-leaf
+consumer share these seats; the new runtime test walks through each opened postern
+and is stopped by each shut one. No first-fort wicket inference is borrowed.
+
+The nine canonical cameras now live in
+`data/reference_views/fort_dearborn_blockhouse/` and the separately named1855
+quarters view in `data/reference_views/fort_dearborn_commandants_quarters/`. Panel5 retains every number of the
+existing T-3040 world camera and all21 members. The other panoramic review frames
+re-anchor the actual existing Eastman/Kinzie camera through world coordinates, then
+fit only horizontal extent and image centre; their original geography is not silently
+replaced by a fort-specific invented historical station. The Kellogg close-up is an
+explicit bounded, later-form diagnostic. All are `diagnostic_only`: no invented
+“From this spot” invitation. Common grade, analytical overcast light and source-pixel
+framing are not historical terrain or lighting. Every new render must bind actual
+current assets and placements; the old held cupola pair remains historical.
+
+## Which evidence governs
+
+Harrison's1830 plan, with its stated retrospective additions and approximate scale,
+and Hubbard's1827 arrangement control named positions. They agree building by building.
+A compressed1893 panorama or a weak camera fit cannot overrule those positions. The
+1855 key supplies the existing stated quarters dimensions, as an explicitly later
+continuity inference. The model keeps its existing footprint disagreement rather than
+stretching the officers' range from60ft to the plan's approximately80ft to fit a picture.
+
+Direct collation of actual1881p43, explicitly captioned1850, finds the same ordered
+foreground masses in Kurzpanel5: left low shed, gallery, tallgable with external stair,
+tall-chimney range, tinygable and cupola blockhouse. Kurz omits the1850MarineHospital
+and right lighthouse/keeper context, compresses spacing and recolours the scene.
+Dependence/compositional adaptation is inferred from the actual pictures, not a
+separately documented engraving genealogy. Its “rebuilt1835” caption therefore does
+not independently date those forms toJuly1835. The1830plan and dated text control.
+
+Kurz panel5 draws a galleried range and an adjacent range with external stairs, but
+neither is keyed. They are **not assigned to arbitrary named records**. The gallery
+already built on the officers' quarters rests on Hubbard, not on that assignment.
+The blockhouse and pointed palisade identify securely; the cameras give only the
+palisade a `card_members` image credit. Context enrollment attests none of the others.
+
+The keyed Wau-Bun1831 reproduction and its unkeyed companion are the same dependent
+witness family. Wentworth1881 pp.86–87 also prints Hubbard's criticism of the high
+ground, river bends and blockhouse height. They supply bounded relative forms, not
+independent metric dimensions or proof every building survived unchanged to1835.
+The small keyed “Wash-house” does not uniquely identify the one plan-based shed:
+Hubbard describes several on the beach and the plan names one farther inland.
+Nor is the keyed Gen.Beaubien residence automatically the separate U.S.Factor's House.
+
+Schoolcraft/Eastman (scene1820, print1854) and Childs (view1820, caption1818–1830,
+print1857 per the inventory) show the earlier second fort. Their similar compositions
+are not newly counted as independent eyewitnesses; earlier barracks are not assumed
+to be July1835 fabric. Castelnau (scene circa1838, publication1842) supplies a later
+harbour cross-check. Kellogg/Blanchard (made1856, scene approximately1836–1849) is
+later despite its misleading local filename ending in1830. Its louvres, adjacent
+small projection, later fence and completed Lake House are not copied backwards.
+
+The three held Getty/Alamy/Hindman previews were actually opened for coverage and
+identity only. They supply no geometry, camera, texture or new licensed asset.
+The modern Chicagology reproductions remain `check_required`. Actual1881printed
+p43 andp92/p93were acquired directly from InternetArchive and visually read, with
+PDscansheld under `data/sources/assets/second_fort_wentworth_1881/`. They now have
+separate later-state diagnostics. p93securely names commandantsA andofficersB; A
+shows a two-level front gallery, Bshows the already-built officers gallery. This
+settles their1855identities without declaring everyfitting unchangedinJuly1835.
+The1850/1855board fence and enlargedparade remain laterstate. Actualp93prints
+parade80×250ft, correcting the old200fttranscription; the1835plan court is unchanged. No held reproduction is promoted by the age of its underlying artwork.
+
+## The complete 21-member disposition
+
+“Occluded” in the matrix means the named interior member is hidden or cannot be
+separated confidently from the unkeyed overlapping ranges. It is not a positive
+identification of a particular printed roof. “Not shown” means no individually
+assignable image feature; it does not claim the historical building did not exist.
+
+| Record suffix | Finite architectural disposition |
+|---|---|
+| artillery_house | Retain plan/text east-side building; no uniquely identified picture roof. |
+| barracks | Retain east soldiers range and galleryfalse; do not transfer an unidentified gallery or earlier barracks. |
+| big_barn | Keep plan-based body; build its explicitly named cupola at declared reconstructed shape/dimensions. |
+| blockhouse | Keep delivered square cupola and centre stack0; plan controls footprint, later roof details excluded. |
+| commandants_quarters | Retain north brick range and stated25×50ft body; adopt keyed1855Afront double gallery as explicit RECON continuity, preserving all15openings and moving only new supports clear of trim. |
+| flagstaff | Staff occurs in earlier/Wau views; no picture establishes its precise height or flag. |
+| garrison_garden | Plan/text garden retained; already-built flora planting acknowledged, stale absence note corrected; no duplicate trees. |
+| guard_house | Plan/Hubbard west-of-south-gate assignment retained. |
+| magazine | Brick store between guard/blockhouse retained; small printed gable not uniquely keyed. |
+| officers_quarters | Existing west log range and double piazza retained; build explicit exterior stair with reconstructed side/run. |
+| out_building_a | Unnamed plan building retained at reconstructed form. |
+| out_building_b | Unnamed plan building retained at reconstructed form. |
+| palisade | Keep pointed stockade and two large main gates; add the distinct small posterns at two reconstructed clear side seats. Later rough board fence excluded. |
+| parade | Retain stockaded court; do not backdate later enlarged parade. |
+| root_house | Retain attested earth-cellar class; no individually identified image cellar. |
+| root_house_b | Retain explicitly reconstructed second cellar; no picture asserts a count of two. |
+| shop | Named plan shop retained; no arbitrary panorama house assignment. |
+| store_house | East-of-south-gate assignment retained; no individual unkeyed roof identity. |
+| sutlers_store | North-east plan/text store retained; no arbitrary bay/stack transfer. |
+| us_factors_house | Retain independent identity; no transfer from disputed keyed Beaubien residence. |
+| wash_house | Keep plan-based shed; keyed1831 small house is a dated class/context comparison. |
+
+Beyond these four explicitly fixed omissions, no additional physical error of more
+than0.3m, missing element, wrong count or wrong
+material has been established for a securely identified July1835 building in this
+corpus. Cross-date disagreements, unidentified ranges, retrospective composition,
+source-pixel offsets and camera alternatives are adjudicated under AGENTS rule11 /
+T-3153; they do not become an endless list of new architectural blockers. Actual
+new side-by-sides still require visual review before any `matches` verdict.
+
+## Validation and delivery boundary
+
+The CPU stair geometry test measures emitted tread levels, ground-to-floor risers,
+landing clearance, run, rail height and guarded invalid combinations. The actual
+postern runtime CPU test checks four rendered leaves, unchanged main-gate spans,
+closed barriers, real interaction swings and actual walker passage at both side seats.
+Existing fort
+front tests pass, including legacy16 positional parameters, five first-fort canopy
+joints and Float32 contact. Pinned native generation and current actual comparisons
+are integrated by the root; this source parcel does not invent those receipts.
+
+The two contained Wentworth cuts have their own credited illustration source records,
+with1881publication and1850/1855depiction stated separately. The book remains the
+historical text citation. Actual `compile_pictures.derive` output confirms the1850
+cut reaches the blockhouse card and the1855cut reaches commandantsA/officersB, with
+creator, holder, URL and rights, and without an invented historical spot. This is
+compiler proof; published phone/desktop credit visibility remains the root’s UI check.
+
+The native gate reader now resolves per-side settings through the actual pure
+parameter API. It retains native gateway closure and independently measures the
+full wicket opening through every MASTER material. Runtime leaves are explicit
